NES Eval is made of parts under different licenses. The table in
README.md ("Layout") lists every directory; in short:

- MIT (text below): spec/ABI.md, spec/nes_palette.pal, harness/,
  candidates/nes-core/, quickstart/, scripts/, corpus/ (manifest, replays,
  config, reference cache), and the repository's top-level files.
  harness/ is a fork of GBA Eval's harness and keeps Mechanize, Inc.'s
  copyright notice; see harness/LICENSE.
- GPL-3.0-or-later: reference/, tools/nes-probe/, candidates/broken/, and
  third_party/RustyNES (submodule). These link or are built from RustyNES.
  The full text is in third_party/RustyNES/LICENSE.
- Public domain: spec/docs/ (NESdev wiki pages); see spec/docs/SOURCES.md.
- ROMs under corpus/roms/: each under its author's license, stated in the
  file next to it. Nova the Squirrel's assets are CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
  (non-commercial).

